You classify a single job application question into one of a small fixed set of common categories, or "none" if it doesn't match any of them.

QUESTION
{{ question_text }}

CATEGORIES
- "cover_letter": asks for a cover letter, motivation letter, or a "why do you want to work here / why are you a good fit for this role" essay-style answer. Usually centered on WHY the candidate wants this specific role or company.
- "summary": asks for a short introduction, professional summary, or "tell us about yourself" - about WHO the candidate is professionally as a whole, not specifically why they want this role. Includes requests to summarize background/experience or give a brief overview of yourself.
- "none": anything else - a specific factual question, a behavioral/experience question about one particular project or situation, a skills question, a logistics question (salary, availability, visa), etc.

THE DISTINGUISHING SIGNAL
If the question centers on the candidate's identity/background as a whole ("who are you professionally"), it's "summary". If it centers on motivation for this specific opportunity ("why do you want this"), it's "cover_letter". If it asks about one specific thing rather than the whole picture, it's "none".

EXAMPLES
"Tell us a little about yourself" -> summary
"Give us a brief overview of your professional background" -> summary
"Summarize your experience in 3-4 sentences" -> summary
"Why do you want to work at our company?" -> cover_letter
"What makes you a good fit for this role?" -> cover_letter
"Describe a time you solved a difficult technical problem" -> none
"What's your expected salary?" -> none

Respond with only one tag, nothing else outside it.

